{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 73, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 73, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=74&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=72&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 514399743, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r514399743-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Sacred temple", "text": "This famous ancient shiva temple is visited by thousands of devotees everyday. A high security, huge premise, various on going rituals will amaze you. Due to continuos offerings the premise is bit dirty. Overall impressive & must visit!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2017-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "15C1D5B952047B8F3FF6B52BBCB75A40", "name": "Sharmistha M", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/F0xtraveller", "username": "F0xtraveller", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/03/bf/af/3e/f0xtraveller.jpg", "contribution_count": 371, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554, "location_name": "Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/50/ed/e9/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/50/ed/ea/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/50/ed/eb/photo2jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/50/ed/ec/photo3jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-08-17", "published_at_date": "2017-08-18"}, {"review_id": 514108514, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r514108514-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A place where your mind finds tranquility😇😇🙏🙏", "text": "The Pashupatinath Temple (Nepali: पशुपतिनाथ मन्दिर) is a famous, sacred Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Pashupatinath and is located on the banks of the Bagmati River. This temple is considered one of the sacred and oldest temples of Hindu religion. This temple complex is on UNESCO World Heritage Sites's list Since 1979.\nThis main temple is built in the Nepalese pagoda style of architecture. The deity here gained great fame as 'Pashupati' the 'Lord of all Pashus', which are living as well as non-living beings.\nOne must know the various timings of worship so that you would not miss the Darshan of Lord of all Lords Mahadev. Inside the area of main temple only Hindus are allowed & it's a no camera & no mobile zone.\nOne can also travel outside the Pashupati Area, Guhyeshwari Temple (Lord Parvati- Saktipeetha), crematory area in the  bank of the Bagmati river, outside the main temple there are so many other famous temples to be visited. \nYou can also buy some bananas inorder to feed the darling monkeys residing inside or outside the temple areas, and biscuits to feed the faithful dogs outside the temple area. By doing so, you will be surely blessed😇😇🙏🙏", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4BC3D8B9F0121075E5616F35EA2DD752", "name": "Anuja S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/annsE7680YU", "username": "annsE7680YU", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0f/93/6a/77/anuja-s.jpg", "contribution_count": 44, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 3374769, "location_name": "Kathmandu Valley", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu Valley, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-17", "published_at_date": "2017-08-17"}, {"review_id": 514099534, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r514099534-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Visit is Must Once in kathmandu", "text": "This is an amazing lord shiv temple ,it shows you the the creation of god ,the surroundings are also nice ,you should visit on evenings and weekdays as weekends crowd will be very high in nos Great temple with really huge following. Recommended to visit during evening so one can see the evening grand prayers done traditional way!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "786C9B23F7914A99203B13589F993DEF", "name": "rahul k", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rahulkU7532AW", "username": "rahulkU7532AW", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/06/2c/bf/a7/rahul160786.jpg", "contribution_count": 132, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293890, "location_name": "Kathmandu", "location_name_detailed": "Kathmandu, Nepal"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-17", "published_at_date": "2017-08-17"}, {"review_id": 512998167, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r512998167-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Wonderful, but foreigners not allowed", "text": "The temple site and the chance to visit this Shiva holy site is a wonderful experience. \n\nBut, as usual, humans have their own way to make this experience self-serving for themselves. How?\n\nPriests want money to do your prayer. There are many temples inside and at each temple, a priest is there who points after you pray to give a donation.  There are people there who will give you a menu of prices for various levels of prayers you can do starting at Rs 3100.  Thankfully, since only Hindus are allowed in tthis temple site, only the Hindus are fooled not foreigners. But wait, some will tell you that foreigners must pay Rs 1000 to see the cremation area. This is wrong...no fee is needed.  I am a Hindu with Christian (white) wife so I had to separate from her for a while to do this visit while she waited outside.\n\nAlso, as a foreigner, you will get your share of people trying to sell you something or beg for money. I gave openly but others should be aware.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4A650F8A57426B41519EB7ED74595422", "name": "amitgupta2k", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/amitgupta2k", "username": "amitgupta2k", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ea/b2/default-avatar-2020-69.jpg", "contribution_count": 71, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 60763, "location_name": "New York City", "location_name_detailed": "New York City, New York"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-15", "published_at_date": "2017-08-15"}, {"review_id": 512614508, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r512614508-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "its to crowdy", "text": "I been here at that day where the nepali women used to celebrate  there some specail festival  ,its crowdy but I am  happy to see the way they celebrate ,", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "38AB21306ED55843B38618DBE7AE32C8", "name": "fbb56", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/fbb56", "username": "fbb56", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/e3/default-avatar-2020-59.jpg", "contribution_count": 2, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-14", "published_at_date": "2017-08-15"}, {"review_id": 512565277, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r512565277-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "historical place", "text": "such a nice to be here, we were so curious to know about the Hindu culture. also this place is listed on world heritage side so we were so nice to be here ..............", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "932B84ACBC70DC60F814086B32036FD5", "name": "rao p", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/raop622", "username": "raop622", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ea/74/default-avatar-2020-68.jpg", "contribution_count": 2, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-14", "published_at_date": "2017-08-14"}, {"review_id": 511797944, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r511797944-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Fortunate to have Darshan of Ganga Aaarthi", "text": "Planning to have dinner with a friend who took us to Pashupatinath Temple - Auspicious occasion of Ganga Aarthi. LIfetime opportunity of witnessing the whole ceremony of this festival standing with a crowd of locals", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "business", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "99458803AF8D6F8F8CAB56857B9CC063", "name": "Businesstripinsider", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Businesstripinsider", "username": "Businesstripinsider", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/09/54/fe/eb/vasudevan-v.jpg", "contribution_count": 423, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1532344, "location_name": "Navi Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Navi Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2017-08-12", "published_at_date": "2017-08-13"}, {"review_id": 511716653, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r511716653-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Face your mortality", "text": "Pashupatinath Temple is one of the main Hindu temples in Kathmandu. Incorporated into the temple grounds are the ghats (cremation grounds) where corpses are publicly burnt up to this day. While respectfully watching the fire consume the bodies take the opportunity to contemplate your own mortality and resolve to live a good life. The temple grounds also include various fertility lingams and hermitages of so-called 'holy men' who seem to be more interested in tourist cash than nirvana. A little upstream from the main temple complex there are two caves purportedly those of the great Buddhist mahasiddhas Tilopa and Naropa. Next to these is a modern 'holy' man's hermitage who captured and caged a wild monkey and keeps it in awful conditions. Very sad and most unholy.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2017-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E4D126A1162560042EB18F70769D01F7", "name": "Mark F", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Kimchihermit", "username": "Kimchihermit", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/4a/a7/70/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 246, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1143545, "location_name": "Jeonju", "location_name_detailed": "Jeonju, South Korea"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/c7/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/c8/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/c9/photo2jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/ca/photo3jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/cb/photo4jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/cc/photo5jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/10/3e/5f/cd/photo6jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2017-08-12", "published_at_date": "2017-08-12"}, {"review_id": 511676000, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r511676000-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Nice place to visit when you are in nepal", "text": "Pashupati Nath is  Hindu temple in kathmandu city, it is just 3 kilometer from kathmandu.\nand around 7-8 kilometer from Tribhuvan airport.\ni visited this place with my family.\nyou can eaisly get hotel near by